    "company_name": "Aardaia2026🇳🇱WageningenNetherlandsActive",
    "company_url": "https://aardaia.com/",
    "description": "Introducing AardakerA new kind of protein crop.Protein is the world's most expensive macronutrient to produce because it depends on nitrogen. Synthetic nitrogen fertilizer is energy-intensive to manufacture, volatile in price, and environmentally damaging to apply.Legume crops solve this problem by fixing nitrogen from the air, making them naturally rich in protein. But most produce far less biomass per hectare than the world's highest-yielding crops.Tuber crops like potato and cassava are among agriculture's highest-yielding crops, but they contain relatively little protein.Aardaker combines both systems: the yield potential of a tuber with the nitrogen biology of a legume.Young aardaker plant in the fieldFixes its own nitrogen. Forms edible tubers. Naturally protein-rich.No GMO, no biotech, no synthetic fertilizer: just a species with the right biology, selected and domesticated for a modern protein system.",
